    "hp_about_story": {
      "type": "hp-about-story",
      "blocks": {
        "point_1": {
          "type": "point",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "gem",
            "title": "Designed to Belong Together",
            "text": "Build your entire table around complementary aesthetics. Our collections are designed to mix, match and layer beautifully, so every piece feels part of a considered whole."
          }
        },
        "point_2": {
          "type": "point",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "sparkles",
            "title": "Inspired by Everywhere",
            "text": "From the timeless character of Windsor to the sun-soaked charm of Limone, our collections take inspiration from different places, moods and traditions around the world — each with a personality of its own."
          }
        },
        "point_3": {
          "type": "point",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "shield-check",
            "title": "Curated for Every Table",
            "text": "From everyday family meals to intimate gatherings, special events and restaurants, our curated themes make it easy to create a table that feels intentional, memorable and entirely your own."
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "point_1",
        "point_2",
        "point_3"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/WhatsApp_Image_2026-04-19_at_7.42.31_PM.webp",
        "image_2": "shopify://shop_images/serveware-thp.webp",
        "flip": false,
        "bg_color": "#fff9df",
        "badge_value": "Est. 2024",
        "badge_label": "Islamabad, Pakistan",
        "badge_color": "#1a4b46",
        "eyebrow": "Chapter One — The Beginning",
        "heading": "Where Global Inspiration Meets the Pakistani Table",
        "text": "<p>The Home Palette started in 2024 with a simple ambition: to bring a level of ceramic tableware to Pakistan that had never been offered here before. At the time, finding truly handcrafted, A-grade ceramics with a premium finish meant looking beyond Pakistan. We saw a gap and decided to fill it.</p><p>Today, The Home Palette is built around bringing premium, beautifully crafted tableware closer to home. What began as an idea has grown into partnerships with multiple factories and workshops across the country, supported by trained artisans and an in-house design team. </p><p>Every day, our pieces make their way into thousands of homes, bringing colour, character, and considered design to the table.</p>",
        "quote": "A table should look like the people who set it — warm, colourful, and entirely their own.",
        "sign_name": "The Home Palette",
        "sign_role": "Paradise Commercial, Bahria Town Phase 4",
        "button_label": "Browse Collections",
        "button_link": "shopify://collections"
      }
    },
    "hp_about_manifesto": {
      "type": "hp-about-manifesto",
      "settings": {
        "bg_color": "#fff9df",
        "center_head": true,
        "drop_cap": true,
        "eyebrow": "Chapter Two — Our Core Belief",
        "heading": "A Home Is Made in the Details",
        "lede": "<p>At The Home Palette, we believe that a beautiful home is created through the little details — the pieces you choose, the way you style them, and the moments you create around them.</p>",
        "body": "<p>The Home Palette is a pioneer of handcrafted, premium, and A-grade tableware in Pakistan, bringing together thoughtfully crafted ceramics, woven pieces, metalware, cutlery and wooden accessories, designed to add warmth, character and personality to your spaces.</p><p>But for us, it’s about more than just beautiful products. We’re passionate about supporting local women artisans and celebrating the craftsmanship behind every piece. From hand-finished ceramics to beautifully woven placemats, runners, tissue boxes and accessories, each piece represents skill, creativity, and the hands that bring it to life.</p><p>We believe beautiful tableware should also be made for real living. That’s why we focus on pieces that are safe, durable, functional and made to be enjoyed every day — whether it’s a quiet breakfast at home, a dinner with loved ones, or a table set for a special celebration.</p><p>Today, The Home Palette is loved not only by individuals and families, but also by hotels and restaurants across Pakistan, who choose our pieces to bring a distinctive touch to their spaces and tables.</p><p>From everyday homes to hospitality spaces, we’re proud to be a part of the places where people gather, connect, celebrate and create memories.</p>",
        "quote_lead": "Because we don’t just want to decorate your table",
        "quote": "We want to make every tablescape a moment.",
        "button_label": "Shop the Collections",
        "button_link": "shopify://collections",
        "button_2_label": "For Hospitality",
        "button_2_link": "/pages/hospitality"
      }
    },
    "hp_about_process": {
      "type": "hp-about-process",
      "blocks": {
        "step_1": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/thp-workshop-bowls-drying.jpg",
            "title": "Clay & sourcing",
            "text": "Every batch begins at the workshop, with clay chosen in person rather than ordered from a catalogue. We work with a small number of family-run potteries and buy whole production runs instead of cherry-picking, which is what lets those workshops plan months ahead instead of week to week.",
            "caption": "Greenware on the workshop racks",
            "meta": "Family-run partners",
            "meta_icon": "leaf"
          }
        },
        "step_2": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/thp-workshop-plates-drying.jpg",
            "title": "Shaping & casting",
            "text": "Plates and bowls are thrown on the wheel or slip-cast in plaster moulds, then left to firm up to leather-hard before the foot is trimmed. It is the slowest stage of the whole process, and the one that decides whether a stack of six plates will sit flush on your shelf.",
            "caption": "Cast plates firming up on plaster",
            "meta": "24–48 hours drying",
            "meta_icon": "ruler"
          }
        },
        "step_3": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/thp-workshop-platters-drying.jpg",
            "title": "The first firing",
            "text": "Dried greenware goes into its bisque firing and comes out porous and chalky — strong enough to handle, thirsty enough to take glaze evenly. Anything that warped or cracked is pulled here, before a single rupee of glaze is spent on it.",
            "caption": "Waiting on the racks for the kiln",
            "meta": "≈900°C",
            "meta_icon": "flame"
          }
        },
        "step_4": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Aura-Tea-Set-Reactive-Cloud-Grey-The-Home-Palette-43124399767851.webp",
            "title": "Glaze & colour matching",
            "text": "This is where the palette is actually made. Glazes are mixed in batches and checked against the master tile for each colour — Sage Green, Limone Yellow, Reactive Cloud Grey — so the range stays consistent season after season. Reactive glazes are the deliberate exception: they are allowed to move in the kiln, which is why no two pieces come out identical.",
            "caption": "Matched against the master tile",
            "meta": "14 colour families",
            "meta_icon": "sparkles"
          }
        },
        "step_5": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/IMG-20250612-WA0107_3.webp",
            "title": "Into the kiln",
            "text": "The glost firing takes each piece well past 1,100°C, where the glaze vitrifies into a hard, food-safe surface that survives daily use and the dishwasher. Roughly twelve hours up and twelve hours back down — rush the cooling and the glaze crazes.",
            "caption": "Twelve hours up, twelve hours down",
            "meta": "1,100°C and beyond",
            "meta_icon": "flame"
          }
        },
        "step_6": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/WhatsApp_Image_2026-04-19_at_7.42.31_PM_1.webp",
            "title": "Inspection & packing",
            "text": "Every piece is turned over, tapped for a clean ring, checked for pinholes and measured against the rest of its set. What passes is wrapped in foam sleeves, corner-blocked and boxed in double-wall cartons — which is why breakage is the rarest email in our inbox.",
            "caption": "Wrapped, corner-blocked, double-boxed",
            "meta": "Piece by piece",
            "meta_icon": "shield-check"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "step_1",
        "step_2",
        "step_3",
        "step_4",
        "step_5",
        "step_6"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "bg_color": "#1a4b46",
        "accent_color": "#7dc6bb",
        "flip": false,
        "center_head": true,
        "eyebrow": "Chapter Three — Inside the Workshop",
        "heading": "How a Piece Becomes Part of the Palette",
        "text": "Six stages, most of them done by hand. It is slower than machine production — and it is the reason no two reactive-glaze pieces ever leave the kiln identical.",
        "foot_text": "Pieces that do not pass inspection stay at the workshop. We would rather be short of stock for a week than send out a second as though it were a first.",
        "button_label": "See the Collections",
        "button_link": "shopify://collections"
      }
    },
